{
  "id": "80549",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Calculating Ka and Kb from pH",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Acid-dissociation constants and base-dissociation constants are determined experimentally from pH measurements. We now look at examples of calculating "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "b"
              },
              {
                "text": " values when pH is known. The process is the same as we have used for previous equilibrium calculations but with an additional step to convert pH into concentrations."
              }
            ],
            "id": "yuxumjodgiurw08",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "748449354",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The pH of a 0.0516-M solution of nitrous acid, HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is 2.34 at 25 °C. What is the "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " value for HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at 25 °C?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "z9v0huleprernk6",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "Write the equilibrium reaction and "
                          },
                          {
                            "em": true,
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "K"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "a"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": " expression."
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "1514907971",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1e8uiswqedqs8sn",
                    "type": "li"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vuqpuw36hoz3mlh",
                "type": "ul"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We first write the ionization reaction equation and acid-ionization constant expression for nitrous acid:"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "{\\mathrm{HNO}}_2(aq)+{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)+\\mathrm{NO}_2^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm a}=\\frac{\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{NO}_2^- \\rbrack}{\\lbrack{\\mathrm{HNO}}_2\\rbrack}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "orwhe0kac3is46d",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "Determine [H"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "3"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "O"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "+"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "] from pH."
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "1659338726",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "a9eobkl8cvifexy",
                    "type": "li"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "z6gghycax7hmgmt",
                "type": "ul"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "To determine the values in the ICE (initial, change, equilibrium) table, we need to calculate [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "equil"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", the equilibrium concentration of hydronium ion, from the pH:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "rkxdlvfgoqp4np4",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "r7atxosc91fmc8e",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "g87smvkrn52ap0e",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\;=\\;10^{-\\mathrm{pH}}\\;=\\;10^{-2.34}\\;=\\;0.0046\\;\\mathrm M",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "Complete the ICE table based on initial [HA] and equilibrium [H"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "sub": true,
                            "text": "3"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "O"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "sup": true,
                            "text": "+"
                          },
                          {
                            "strong": true,
                            "text": "]."
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "3937806243",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "m4s73le0evo6tv9",
                    "type": "li"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "nl030v8i21vy9vx",
                "type": "ul"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The initial state is nonionized HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", so [HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "initial"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 0.0516 M and [NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "initial"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "initial"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 0. The initial [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is its concentration in pure water, which is so much less than the equilibrium concentration that we approximate it as zero (~0)."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tjua49tj392r6vo",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The change in concentration of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "x"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is the difference between [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "equil"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which we determined from the pH, and the initial concentration, [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "initial"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "n9zel05bhaebhed",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "For each 1 mol of HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that ionizes, 1 mol H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and 1 mol of NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " are formed, so the change in [NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is equal to the change in [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "]. The equilibrium [HNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is equal to its initial concentration plus the change in its concentration."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "x5mw2c21jtb14b9",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Now we can fill in the ICE table with the concentrations at equilibrium, as shown:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a9rsvljupfmla81",
                "type": "p"
              },
